                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "42556981",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198037259809",
                            "num_reviews": 49,
                            "playtime_forever": 313,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 313,
                            "last_played": 1528022745
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Promising project, but some awkward design decisions prevent me from recommending this in its current state. For full review, see: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5RZlwNWwDhM\n\nPros:\n- Great, cohesive artstyle\n- Interesting premise\n- Nice background music\n- Interesting synergies between robots, enhanced by choices of skills for each individual robot\n\nCons:\n- Too much reliance on buffs/debuffs. It's not uncommon to have 10+ buffs/debuffs added to your characters, making it easy to lose sight of what's happening.\n- 6 enemies in a fight can increase the chaos. Your character might be fine one moment and dead the next, because suddenly many enemies in a row decided to attack that one.\n- Very uninspired trap system. You enter a room, a trap springs, you get damage. You can't do anything about these things.\n- Boring map design. No way to avoid dangers (with rare exceptions).\n- Not a roguelike at all, despite being advertised as such (unless you consider a game like Diablo3 on hardmode a roguelike?)\n- Enemies level with you. This means that if you cannot beat a level, you basically are stuck, because if you grind, the enemies will become stronger as well. You could argue that you should just restart the game (like in roguelikes sometimes) and try again, however, the game is too slow paced and not interesting enough for me to do that. I want to follow the story and do the campaign missions in order, not redo them every time. This game just does not fit that type of repetitive gameloop that traditional roguelikes succeed at.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1528384450,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1528384450,
                        "voted_up": false,
                        "votes_up": 221,
                        "votes_funny": 3,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.7668658494949341,
                        "comment_count": 17,
                        "steam_purchase": false,
                        "received_for_free": true,
                        "written_during_early_access": true,
                        "developer_response": "Thank you for the feedback.\n\nDon't forget that this game is only in Early Access for the moment, so a lot of things are subject to changes and improvements.\n\nAbout buffs/debuffs, we have added a sorting so players can better check them without struggling too much. Also, we've merged some of them into one or completely deleted some others when it was possible, but only a few are concerned. If you don't like games with a lot buffs/debuffs, the issue might still bother you depending on the robot combination and skills you will choose.\n\nThe game was tagged as roguelike because the hardcore difficulty, that has been implemented since then, is a permadeath mode. We've changed the denomination to \"roguelite\" though, to prevent players having too much expectations by seeing \"roguelike\" but that would still play in easy or normal mode instead of hardcore.\n\nFor the enemies level scaling part, we've already made a complete revamp of the mission and enemies level curve. The previous level scaling has been kept for hardcore only.\n\nTrap system has been changed and improved as well.\n\nWe hope that you will give the game a second chance and that it might change your first impressions.\n\nHave fun and take care!\n\nEDIT (02/06/19): For those who are curious about the state of the game, feel free to take a look at the Patch notes in the News section of the game.\n\nThe 1.1 update will be available later today with fixes, adjustments and balancing based on the reports and feedback of our players on the forums, in the reviews section or on our Discord.\n\nTank you all for you interest about the game!",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1549468355,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
